---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Diagram from '../components/Diagram.astro';
const tags = [
  ['v=DMARC1', 'required', 'Protocol version, must be first.'],
  ['p=', 'required', 'Policy for the domain: none, quarantine, or reject.'],
  ['sp=', 'optional', 'Policy for subdomains (defaults to p).'],
  ['pct=', 'optional', '% of failing mail the policy applies to (default 100).'],
  ['rua=', 'recommended', 'mailto: address for aggregate (aggregate) reports.'],
  ['ruf=', 'optional', 'mailto: address for forensic (failure) reports.'],
  ['adkim=', 'optional', 'DKIM alignment: r (relaxed, default) or s (strict).'],
  ['aspf=', 'optional', 'SPF alignment: r (relaxed, default) or s (strict).'],
  ['fo=', 'optional', 'When forensic reports are sent (0, 1, d, s).'],
  ['ri=', 'optional', 'Report interval in seconds (default 86400 = daily).'],
];

---
<BaseLayout title="DMARC Record: Syntax, Tags, and Examples" description="DMARC record syntax: every tag explained (p, sp, pct, rua, ruf, adkim, aspf), worked examples, and how to publish the record."  
 breadcrumb={[["Home", "/"], ["Email Authentication", "/email-authentication/"], ["DMARC Record Syntax"]]}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">DMARC Record Syntax</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">DMARC Record: Syntax and Tags</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      A DMARC record is a TXT record at <code class="font-mono text-accent-soft">_dmarc.yourdomain.com</code>
     , note the underscore, built from semicolon-separated tags. Here is every tag and what it does.
    </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">DMARC identifier alignment scenarios</h2>
    <section class="not-prose my-4" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="pdns-table" style="width:100%">
          <thead><tr><th>Visible From domain</th><th>SPF / DKIM domain</th><th>Relaxed alignment</th><th>Strict alignment</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">example.com</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">example.com (either protocol)</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">PASS</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">PASS</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">example.com</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">mail.example.com</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">PASS (org domain matches)</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">FAIL (not exact)</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">example.com</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">esp-customer.net</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">FAIL</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">FAIL</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">billing.example.com</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">billing.example.com</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">PASS</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">PASS</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">DMARC identifier alignment scenarios</h2>
    <section class="not-prose my-4" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="pdns-table" style="width:100%">
          <thead><tr><th>Visible From domain</th><th>SPF / DKIM domain</th><th>Relaxed alignment</th><th>Strict alignment</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">example.com</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">example.com (either protocol)</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">PASS</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">PASS</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">example.com</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">mail.example.com</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">PASS (org domain matches)</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">FAIL (not exact)</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">example.com</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">esp-customer.net</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">FAIL</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">FAIL</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">billing.example.com</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">billing.example.com</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">PASS</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">PASS</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
    <Diagram name="dmarc-tree" caption="The DMARC decision tree showing policy application" />

    <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60">
      <table class="pdns-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Tag</th><th>Status</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {tags.map(([tag, status, meaning]) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-accent">{tag}</td>
              <td class="text-xs text-ink-faint">{status}</td>
              <td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">{meaning}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="rich-text mt-10">
      <h2>Worked examples</h2>
      <p>Monitoring start:</p>
      <pre class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs text-accent-soft">v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:dmarc@yourdomain.com</pre>
      <p>Enforcement with subdomain policy and ramp:</p>
      <pre class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs text-accent-soft">v=DMARC1; p=reject; sp=reject; pct=100; rua=mailto:dmarc@yourdomain.com; adkim=r; aspf=r</pre>

      <h2>How to publish it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>In your DNS host, create a TXT record with host/name <code>_dmarc</code> (the full name becomes <code>_dmarc.yourdomain.com</code>).</li>
        <li>Paste the record value, build one safely in the <a href="/dmarc-record-generator/">DMARC record generator</a>.</li>
        <li>TTL 3600 is fine; verify with the <a href="/dmarc-record-checker/">DMARC checker</a> minutes later.</li>
        <li>If reports go to a different domain (e.g. a vendor), that domain must authorize yours with an external-report destination record.</li>
      </ul>

      
<h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Where do I publish the DMARC record?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">As a TXT record at _dmarc.yourdomain.com in your authoritative DNS host. Most providers accept the name as _dmarc when you enter it at the root.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I have multiple DMARC records?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No. Exactly one record at _dmarc is valid; multiple records make receivers ignore DMARC entirely. Merge everything into one.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long until DMARC takes effect?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The record propagates in minutes, but receivers cache policies, so expect 24 to 48 hours before the policy is applied everywhere.</p></details></div>
      <h2>Related</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/dmarc/">DMARC: the complete guide</a>, policies, alignment, enforcement road</li>
        <li><a href="/dmarc-report-analyzer/">DMARC report analyzer</a>, free</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
